  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed extension does not comply with the description of development as set out on the submitted application form and therefore does not fall within the parameters of permitted development as set out under Schedule 2, Part 1, Class A of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "The proposed single storey rear extension and the total enlargement would extend beyond a wall forming a side elevation of the original dwellinghouse and would have a width greater than half the width of the original dwellinghouse contrary to Class A.1 (ja) and (j) (iii) of Class A,Part 1, Schedule 2 of the Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) (England) Order 2015 (as amended).",
    "The General Permitted Development Order (GDPO) defines 'detached' in relation to a dwellinghouse as follows :The dwellinghouse does not (a) share a party wall with another building; or (b) have a main wall adjoining the main wall of another building. As a matter of fact and degree, it is considered that the existing extension at no 38 which abuts neighbouring no 40 is a party wall for the purposes of (a) above. This means the  existing extension fails the \"detached\" test as defined by the GPDO and would be considered to be a semi-detached dwellinghouse by default.Therefore, the permitted development rights for detached dwellings is no longer applicable."
  ],
